fajita (OnePlus 6T): Synaptics RMI4 touchscreen over the GENI SE.

Bergamota's touch detector handles Goodix / Novatek / Focaltech; the OnePlus 6T
uses a Synaptics RMI4 (F01/F12) controller at I2C 0x20 on QUPv3 SE12 (i2c@a90000).
This adds a TOUCH_RMI4 kind, a touch_fajita board, and a self-contained fajita
bring-up thread ported from the iOS-16 fajita port: it maps two TLMM tiles
(NORTH for the i2c pins gpio49/50 and reset gpio99, EAST for the 1.8 V switch
gpio88 and ATTN gpio125), votes PM8998 ldoa28, brings up the SE clock, walks the
RMI4 PDT for F01/F12, and polls F12 2D reports, reusing the shared
touch_msg / touch_se_init / touch_report helpers. Board-gated on
sweet_board_fajita() ("oneplus,fajita"); sweet and beryllium are untouched.

Verified: the new functions syntax-check clean against stubbed helpers; the
diff applies on top of the full patches-11215 series. Not yet run on device.

